    "result": "Perfect! Both fixes are in place and all tests pass:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed two issues in the frai-core test suite:\n\n1. **Governance test (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `/src/finetune/index.js` (lines 361-366). The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only in the default export. The constants are still in the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n2. **Evaluation test (`src/eval/index.test.js`)**: Fixed the `toxicityMetric` function signature in `/src/eval/metrics.js` from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms)`. The problem was that `runEvaluations` passes both outputs and references to all metrics, but the old signature treated references as banned terms, incorrectly flagging outputs that matched the references.\n\n**All 28 tests now pass** (8 test files), and all public exports remain functional.",
